# Golden: Phase-7 node 9210 (Option-2 generated lead) -- "funk" style, VarD
# peak section, a |C|F| two-bar change. Locks funk's generated kLeadMotif (the
# new TrackRole::kLead pattern in funk.hpp's kDP, no other section): seed=1402,
# length=3 (the shortest of the four, a short reaffirming stab, not a
# wandering line), center_degree=0 (the root, mirroring the bass's own
# "staccato single-note root-pop" idiom), vel=96, gate=kGateStab,
# idiom_role=kDrums (onset candidates drawn from kDD's own busiest,
# 13-step syncopated kick/snare/hat mask), gm_program=7 (Clavinet -- the
# owner's call for funk's own signature texture over the corpus's stock brass
# stab, see docs/proposals/phase7-9210-motif-generate-option2-leads.md
# section 4.2). Two full bars of VarD exercise BOTH halves of the
# call-and-response repeat policy (motif.hpp's apply_repeat): bar 1 (repeat=0,
# over C) plays the generated phrase verbatim -- the "statement" -- and bar 2
# (repeat=1, over F) applies the seed's own kDiatonicTranspose with a
# repeat-keyed amount -- the "answer". Routes drums/bass/chord1 following
# arranger_band.acmd's own convention, plus `style route lead synth:7` --
# WITHOUT this route the new kLead content never appears in the golden at all
# (the gap this fixture closes). Any accidental change to funk's kLeadMotif or
# to kDD's onset mask moves these notes/ticks and fails this test.
key C major
port open out virt as synth
chord out synth:4
style load funk
style route drums synth:10
style route bass synth:2
style route chord1 synth:3
style route lead synth:7
style section varD
seq new verse
seq add C 1bar
seq add F 1bar
seq loop on
seq play
transport start
advance 7680
quit
